{"name":"Yellow Nile","hex":"#95804a","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"yellow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow hue.","Lacking courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wadi Howar","blocks":[{"text":"Wadi Howar is a wadi in Sudan and Chad."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Map_of_Sudan_%28New%29.jpg/330px-Map_of_Sudan_%28New%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wadi_Howar"},{"title":"Nile","blocks":[{"text":"The Nile is a major north-flowing river in northeast Africa which empties into the Mediterranean Sea. At 7,088 kilometers (4,404 mi) long, it is the longest river in the world, although the volume of water it carries is much smaller than other major rivers such as the Amazon or the Congo. The Nile has played a central role in the environmental, economic, and cultural history of Africa for millennia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Beautiful_nature_along_Nile_River_01.jpg/330px-Beautiful_nature_along_Nile_River_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nile"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Whiteandblueniles.jpg/500px-Whiteandblueniles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Whiteandblueniles.jpg/500px-Whiteandblueniles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The distinct colors of the White Nile (left) and the Blue Nile (right) are visible where they merge to form the main Nile (top left).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWhiteandblueniles.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Assuan-Hochdamm_15.JPG/500px-Assuan-Hochdamm_15.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Assuan-Hochdamm_15.JPG/1280px-Assuan-Hochdamm_15.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Assuan-Hochdamm_15.JPG/500px-Assuan-Hochdamm_15.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Aswan High Dam is located on the main Nile near the border between Egypt and Sudan. Its electrical generators have the capacity to produce 2.1 gigawatts.[43]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAssuan-Hochdamm_15.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Nile_River_and_delta_from_orbit.jpg/500px-Nile_River_and_delta_from_orbit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Nile_River_and_delta_from_orbit.jpg/500px-Nile_River_and_delta_from_orbit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Nile Delta is the large triangular vegetated region at the top of this photograph, where the river empties into the Mediterranean Sea.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANile_River_and_delta_from_orbit.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Lower_Aber_river_and_tributaries.png/500px-Lower_Aber_river_and_tributaries.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Lower_Aber_river_and_tributaries.png/500px-Lower_Aber_river_and_tributaries.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The source of the Blue Nile is Gish Abay at the bottom of the bright line. The river flows north from there to Lake Tana at the top.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALower_Aber_river_and_tributaries.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Hippos_in_their_Natural_Habitat_in_Kazinga_Channel_10.jpg/500px-Hippos_in_their_Natural_Habitat_in_Kazinga_Channel_10.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Hippos_in_their_Natural_Habitat_in_Kazinga_Channel_10.jpg/500px-Hippos_in_their_Natural_Habitat_in_Kazinga_Channel_10.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=